        "title": {
          "en": "A short story"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Meena visited Mamallapuram and admired the shore temple.\n\"The Pallavas built this,\" said her guide."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "Pallava",
          "Chalukya",
          "temple"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "From the 6th to 10th centuries powerful kingdoms ruled. The Pallavas of Kanchipuram built rock-cut and stone temples at Mamallapuram. The Chalukyas of Badami built temples at Aihole and Pattadakal.\nPulakeshin II of the Chalukyas and Narasimhavarman of the Pallavas fought for power in the south.\nTheir art, architecture and inscriptions tell us much about their times."
        }
